  "en": {
    "title": "Econ 101 - Week 3: Supply and Demand",
    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "Demand",
        "kind": "heading"
      },
      {
        "text": "Demand: the quantity of a good buyers are willing and able to buy at each price",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "Law of demand: as price rises, quantity demanded falls (other things equal)",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "Demand shifters: income, tastes, prices of related goods, expectations",
        "kind": "sub"
      },
      {
        "text": "Normal good: demand rises when income rises",
        "kind": "sub"
      },
      {
        "text": "Inferior good: demand falls when income rises",
        "kind": "sub"
      },
      {
        "text": "Supply",
        "kind": "heading"
      },
      {
        "text": "Supply: the quantity sellers are willing and able to sell at each price",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "Law of supply: as price rises, quantity supplied rises",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "Market",
        "kind": "heading"
      },
      {
        "text": "Equilibrium: the price at which quantity demanded equals quantity supplied",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "Shortage: quantity demanded exceeds quantity supplied, below the equilibrium price",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "Surplus: quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded, above the equilibrium price",
        "kind": "point"
      },
      {
        "text": "e.g. coffee price rises -> demand for tea rises (substitutes)",
        "kind": "example"
      },
      {
        "text": "e.g. income rises -> fewer bus rides (inferior good)",
        "kind": "example"
      }
    ],
